WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.310
R{*\c&H9EC3C5&}e{*\c&H9FC4C6&}-{*\c&HA0C5C7&}O{*\c&HA1C6C8&}p{*\c&HA3C7C9&}e{*\c&HA4C8CA&}n{*\c&HA5C9CC&}i{*\c&HA6CACD&}n{*\c&HA7CBCE&}g {*\c&HAACDD0&}S{*\c&HABCED1&}o{*\c&HACCFD2&}on

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.130
Miura Ramen!

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.040
"A second branch will soon be opening in Kibougahana!"

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.110
Seriously?! That's awesome!

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.560
This place is seriously delicious!

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.350
But their first branch is in a neighboring town...

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.370
Soon I'll be able to eat here whenever I want!

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.890
Hey, Erika, you're drooling all over the place!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.490
Oh, it's Miura!

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.090
Miura?

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.180
Congrats!

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.010
Why didn't you tell me you guys were opening a second branch?!

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.500
I'll come and dine here on opening day!

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.140
Don't.{Technically he's saying 'Don't come' but that makes Erika's next line seem bad out of context and also he's being confrontational - I think it works better shorter.}

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.680
Huh? What do you mean, "don't"?

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.520
Hey, why not?!

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.340
Oh, sir!

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.560
Good afternoon!

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.570
Hey, good afternoon.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.960
Oh, Akira, you're heading back too?

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.530
Huh? Hey, come back, Miura!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.060
{OP}

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.250
HeartCatch

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.710
Precure!

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.260
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.260
Now, all together

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.770
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.730
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.350
Within each of our chests,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.020
they begin to sprout

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.700
The seeds of the heart

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.000
are growing

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.610
bit by bit

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.280
Red,

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:37.900
white

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.200
and yellow

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.950
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.370
all varied colors

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.830
that they

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.040
shine so brightly!

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:52.340
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.840
with such care

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.550
will never wither

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.140
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.020
Now, all together

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.520
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.190
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.060
They're always right by our sides

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:14.900
So together

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.740
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.700
bloom even more!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.200
HeartCatch

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.700
Precure!

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.050
Rejected Ramen<i>!</i>

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.050
Rejected Ramen<i>!</i>

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.590
Next! Third!

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.980
Nice job, Miura!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.950
You're really giving it your all!

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.980
Of course I am! A regular isn't allowed to mess up!

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.720
Miura's on the baseball team, huh?

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.400
Yeah. He's been playing since he was in elementary school.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.110
He's become a regular member of the team, huh? {Removed 'Huh' at the start, doesn't flow really well in English.}

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.180
That's amazing!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.130
He hasn't had the time to play that often.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.570
Back when he was a first year, he was just a backup player.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:14.120
Oh, now that I think about it, that was the same year Miura Ramen's first branch opened. {Added the two 'that's and changed the tense of the second phrase slightly to convey meaning better.}

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.610
Is that so?

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.380
Yeah.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:23.390
Back then, he was advertising, telling everyone he met that his dad had opened a ramen store.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.930
He was really rooting for him, saying, "My dad's ramen is seriously tasty!"

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.980
And then he just tells me not to come...

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.230
What's the matter with him?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.860
I'm home!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.520
Welcome back!

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.530
So which are we using?

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.450
If we're going for color coordination, we should really go with this, right?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.030
But I think this one would be better...

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.620
Is that an opening present for Miura Ramen?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.830
Yeah, but we're having trouble getting it just right...

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.920
We want it to give a real "Congrats on your opening!" feeling...

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.800
That's right. We need it to give off a really cheerful feeling...

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:03.930
Hey.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.050
Hm?

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:04.760
Congratulations on your 2nd Branch!!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.050
Congratulations on your 2nd Branch!!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.680
Here!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.100
Rapeseed blossoms?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.380
Try putting them in!

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.390
Okay...

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.150
Wow! It gives off a "Spring has come!" effect!

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.570
Really makes you want to give it your all...

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.390
That's our daughter for you!

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.090
Thank you, Tsubomi!

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.100
All right! Let's start over with the rapeseed blossoms as our focus!

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.730
Right! Let's make this have a real uplifting, encouraging feel!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.290
<i>Miura...</i>

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.920
<i>Why can't you root for him... {This line doesn't show up even though it's spoken. Why is it hidden?}</i>

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.550
Good afternoon...

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.430
Tsubomi, come out here for a sec! {Added 'come' and for.'}

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.430
Look at this! Something's happened to Coffret!

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.330
It's like he's totally worn out!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.100
Me... too...

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.300
I'm... exhausted...

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.270
What's happened to you two?!

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.240
Well, we're...

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.840
...starviiiing.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.450
Found it!

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.730
What is this?

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.960
It's the Cure Frumix!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.210
First, press that button!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.710
Um... this one?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.800
Next you have to shake it!

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.290
Like this?

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.860
You need to do it harder!

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.330
Like this?!

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.280
That's totally no good!

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.400
Give it here.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.470
How's thiiiiiis?!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.740
That's okay!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.560
This rich texture!

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.940
This addictive taste!

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.570
It's so delicious!

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.220
I'm so happy!

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.380
I totally get it!

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.860
Delicious things really do make you happy!

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.080
Miura Ramen embodies that perfectly!

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.100
The pork with just a hint of the bonito 
flavoring—it's so rich, yet also refreshing... {Changed 'but' to 'and' - that's the actual saying - and reworded the punctuation to work better.}

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.440
Lord Coupe? {LONG ARMS}

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.950
He's trying to encourage you to "Fight!"

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.570
Huh?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.810
Here you go.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.280
Thank you very much!

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:33.330
There's someone that you want to
 encourage too, isn't there, Tsubomi? {Combined 'some' and 'one' into one word.}

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.080
Huh? I don't really...

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.750
Really?

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.890
This is delicious! What kind of tea is it?

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:43.920
It's a herbal tea made with thyme.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.760
In the language of flowers, thyme means "courage."

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.930
<i>Courage...</i>

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.240
Oh, look, it's the horrible son.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.440
I hope he's not going to damage the flowers.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.520
<i>Miura... and his father...</i>

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:26.960
<i>Fight!</i>

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.110
Right!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.240
Tsubomi?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.030
U-Um...

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.650
Um, Miura?

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:44.150
Um...

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.910
U-Um...

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:47.650
Excuse me!

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:54.370
Tsubomi!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.660
Are you okay, Tsubomi?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.030
It hurts...

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.800
You're bleeding...

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.220
Here, have this.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:01.660
Huh?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.660
I'm on the baseball team, after all.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.080
I always carry these around.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.420
Thank you very much...

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.150
Bye.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.070
Um!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.890
Um... Well, you see...

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:18.060
Make sure you put that on, all right?

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:22.690
W-Wait! Miura, what is it you want from your father?!

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.230
Why can't you support his new store?! {Changed 'him' to 'his.'}

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:29.360
Do you want your father to quit running his ramen store?! {Changed 'diner' to 'store' to be consistent. Plus, in Americaland, a diner is a very specific type of eatery.}

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.320
Of course I don't!

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.080
That's way too high!

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.000
Nice catch!

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.880
All right, one more time!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.940
A father and son playing catch, huh? {Catchball? Really? In America we call that 'catch.' Edited.}

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.810
Miura, you used to play catch a lot with your dad too, didn't you?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.560
Yeah, in the past.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.600
Dad!

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.560
Look! I'm definitely gonna become a regular!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.960
All right then!

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.020
I'll definitely come to cheer you on!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.480
You'd better! That's a promise, okay?!

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.740
It wasn't just about playing catch... {Added 'playing,' changed 'catchball' to 'catch.'}

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.470
He would always come to my games...

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.080
And then...

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.450
And then?

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.710
If you don't tell us, we won't understand!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.880
Even if I did, it wouldn't do any good.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.120
Sheesh! This pisses me off!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.300
His Flower of the Heart seemed really dreary...

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.830
Miura...

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:50.980
First Sasorina, and now even you have been defeated by the Precure.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.230
Would you like to explain yourself, Kumojacky?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.100
I was merely attempting to measure their strength.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.840
Next time, I'll surely...

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.610
Is that meant to be an excuse?

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:01.660
Lights!

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:10.380
You manage to be not only repugnant, but repulsive too, Kumojacky. {Changed 'not just' to 'not only.'}

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.790
Flaunting yourself again, Kobraja?

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.580
You're not needed here.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:15.340
Get lost!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:19.050
Au contraire. I'm sure I'll perform much better than you.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.620
Then go, Kobraja.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.180
Defeat the Precure.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.980
Leave it all to me.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.320
Good morniiiiing!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.900
How long are you gonna sleep?! Get up already!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.330
But there's no school today...

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:51.500
It's the grand opening of Miura Ramen's second branch!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.840
You can't just lie in bed all day!

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.580
But it doesn't open until 11...

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.650
If we get in line first, we'll be the first ones to eat! {Yes, yes, I know. Queue, line. But bear with me. I'll give you 'lie in.'}

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:10.210
Oh, Akira! Are you off to practice?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.290
Yeah.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.770
Good timing! Come in for a second.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:19.610
Yo.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:22.240
We just finished up the first batch.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:31.330
If this second branch goes well,
 there'll be a third branch before long!

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:37.960
We've got to work hard and make your dad's dream to let everyone experience Miura Ramen come true!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:38.740
Right!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.020
What's the matter?

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.420
It'll get cold.

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.060
I don't want to eat it!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.850
What's the matter? Are you feeling sick? {Changed 'unwell' to 'feeling sick.'}

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:04.110
Your dad's ramen is full of nutrients, so it'll perk you right up in no time!

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.380
I said I don't want it!

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.880
Non, non! That's no good!

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:21.170
None of these will do...

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.550
Ah, how long must I wander before I find a backdrop that suits me? {Changed 'befits' to 'suits.'}

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.720
What's this? O-ho!

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:33.850
At first glance these flowers seem gaudy, yet they give the building this refined, elegant look...

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.540
This shall do nicely!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.310
Camera!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.130
C'était magnifique.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.960
It's not that you don't like the ramen, right?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.000
So if there's something you want to say, then say it.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.920
Even if I did, it wouldn't make any difference!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.020
After all, your ramen's the most important thing to you, right?!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:12:59.710
Akira!

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.340
You there.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.810
How your heart withers with such delicious suffering.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:18.280
Flower of the Heart, your moment has come!

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.730
Now, let us begin the show!

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:36.430
Desertrian, that's your cue!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.320
Look over there!

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.510
Meeeeeeen!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.130
A Desertrian!

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.110
Tsubomi!

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:48.970
Right!

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.650
Go, Seeds of the Precure!

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.990
Precure!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.960
Open My Heart!

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:56.390
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.600
Cure Blossom!

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:07.210
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:11.650
Cure Marine!

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:19.020
HeartCatch Precure!

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.360
So you're here, Precures.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.730
A new commander of the Desert Apostles...

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.070
Name yourself!

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.410
My name is Kobraja...

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.200
A pleasure to make your acquaintance!

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.090
Blossom!

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.050
Miura!

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.110
What on earth is this?!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:46.880
You always came to cheer for me when I was in elementary school.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:47.940
Huh?

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:51.340
But now, it's just ramen all day every day!

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.430
You don't care about me anymore! {Does this font not have single quotes? There's nothing visible in the "don't."}

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:56.760
Don't!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.970
Men!

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.320
Leave this to us!

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.560
Men! Ramen!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.120
Meeeeeeeeeen!

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:41.850
Dad cares more about his work than me.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:42.850
That's not...

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.140
That's not true!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.820
I hate ramen... and I hate you, Dad!

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:51.970
That ramen store should just disappear!

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:55.570
No!

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.170
Blossom!

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.140
Stop it...

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.940
You mustn't destroy the ramen store!

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.920
You mustn't destroy Dad's dream!

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.340
But just a second ago, he wanted to destroy it!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:23.210
Both of them are part of his true feelings! {Changed 'parts' to 'part' to fix subject-verb agreement.}

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:26.270
He's struggling with those two sets of conflicting emotions.

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.770
<i>Miura...</i>

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:32.210
<i>Because you care about your father...</i>

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:35.070
<i>And you don't want to trouble him when he's working so hard...</i>

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:39.440
<i>You couldn't tell him how much you wanted him to cheer you on...</i>

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.100
His Flower of the Heart was withering from something like that...

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.420
How weak and pathetic he is.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.270
It's not weakness!

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:56.240
It's his kindness!

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.810
Manipulating and trampling on it like that is just cruel!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.800
I've...

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.640
had it up to here with this!

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:08.080
Me too! I'm really annoyed and like...

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.530
Dang it, I can't think of a catchphrase!

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.690
I'll come up with something for next time!

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:13.480
Let's go!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:25.080
Gather, Floral Power!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.480
Blossom Tact!

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.430
Marine Tact!

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:41.580
Gather, Dual Floral Power!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:47.470
Precure Floral Power Fortissimo!

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.360
Heart Catch!

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:14.500
Safe!

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:19.750
Not bad at all.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:21.980
I think we'll leave things here for today.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:22.930
Adieu!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.270
Thank you for the meal!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:35.860
Thank you very much!

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:37.690
Ya know...

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:42.420
Shouldn't we tell them how Miura is feeling?

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.420
No.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:48.200
These things are better coming from the source, I think.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:52.160
It's the source!

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:54.650
Hey, the thing is...

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:58.370
Th-Th-Thanks for the food!

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.220
Dad... I...

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.730
Akira... let's go play catch. {HeartCatchball to catch.}

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:22.700
Let's go.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:27.800
Dad's been waiting with his glove for you. {You use a singular baseball glove.}

00:20:29.650 --> 00:20:31.710
You've got a match next week, right?

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.330
I'll come and cheer you on!

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.420
It doesn't matter, really.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.330
You've got the shop to worry about, right?

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:42.670
That's no good.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:47.680
Expanding Miura Ramen may be my dream... {I know Japanese does this third-person thing, but it doesn't translate well to English. Edited.}

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:51.890
but coming to cheer you on at your baseball games is also my dream! {Works better here though in terms of conversational flow.}

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.860
I promised you back then, didn't I?

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:59.270
That when you became a regular, I'd come cheer you on, Akira.

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.820
You remembered... that promise?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:04.280
Of course I did!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:07.550
Like I'd forget a promise between us men! {Fixed tense from I'll to I'd.}

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.960
Do your best! Cause your dad's gonna cheer with all he's got! {Added 'your.'}

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.920
You too! Do your best with the second branch!

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.080
Right!

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:20.980
Dad!

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:24.970
I'm sorry...

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:26.260
I know!

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:32.850
Miura's Flower of the Heart is lively again!

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:36.650
In the language of flowers, sage means "familial love." {Is this the first time they mention 'salvia?' I was expecting RAPESEED.}

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:41.570
I think a Heart Seed is going to be born...

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:54.300
Playing catch sure is nice. {Changed catchball to playing catch.}

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:55.430
Isn't it?

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:57.960
We've done something good here.

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:09.960
{ED}

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:18.980
HeartCatch!

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:21.900
HeartCatch!

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:24.820
HeartCatch!

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:27.780
HeartCatch Precure!

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:36.330
The flower blooms with an "Open sesame!"

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:39.290
In the wardrobe of my heart

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:42.460
are all the things that a girl loves

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:44.920
Look, they're packed in so tight

00:22:45.470 --> 00:22:48.300
My makeover was a huge success

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:50.890
thanks to this scrunchie and this frilly tunic!

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.890
Our girly showtime

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:56.730
is about to begin!

00:22:57.230 --> 00:22:59.940
Is my coordination lookin' good today?

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.860
Shuffle! Colorful! Beautiful!

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:05.780
Mismatches are just part of my character v(^^)v

00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:07.320
We're pretty

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:09.120
at full bloom!

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.240
If you polish your heart

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:15.290
until it shines

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:16.830
Then even the darkness

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:21.080
will become a guiding light

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:24.090
So don't sulk

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:27.010
because a smile's the best!

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:30.470
Let's make them bloom, facing the sun

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:33.680
The flowers of our hearts

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:36.560
HeartCatch!

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:40.020
HeartCatch Precure!

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:46.000
<i>There's some super in-depth reporting on the current Precure craze!</i>

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:50.030
<i>Kanae's journalist soul reveals the truth behind the Precure's identities...</i>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.280
<i>Wait, what?!</i>

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:52.530
<i>If our identities are exposed, what'll happen?</i>

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:54.030
<i>Horrible, horrible things!</i>

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:55.330
<i>What horrible things?</i>

00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:57.330
<i>Huh? Well... that's a secret!</i>

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:59.870
<i>Tch... Well, I don't mind if you want to keep it a secret.</i>

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:02.580
HeartCatch Precure<i>:</i>

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:06.170
Scoop<i>!</i> The Precures'

00:24:02.580 --> 00:24:06.170
Scoop<i>!</i> The Precures'

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:08.500
<i>We'll catch everyone's hearts!</i>
